  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cross-border investment in water management, climate security and peacebuilding in Mauritania, Mali and Senegal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Planned over a period of twenty-four (24) months, the project aims to use water as an entry point to consolidate peace in the border areas of Mali, Mauritania, and Senegal. Its overall objective is to address key fragility factors related to water use in these border regions by strengthening resource management to ensure sustainable, inclusive, and peaceful access for both sedentary and mobile communities (including transhumant and displaced populations). At the same time, it seeks to support communities&#x2019; adaptive capacities to climate shocks and hazards in order to prevent conflicts and foster peacebuilding</narrative>
  </description>
